 "method": {
  "rs": "Weekly bars: each sector's sessions are grouped by ISO week and the last session of the week is the weekly close. RS = derived sector index / NEPSE index at each weekly close. Sector indices are equal-weight constituent composites (data/sector-indices.json keystone, extended in-memory from the OHLC archive between the keystone's weekly appends); the NEPSE benchmark is the official index (data/index-history.json), last close on or before the sector's weekly close.",
  "rs_ratio": "RS-Ratio = 100 x (RS / SMA13w(RS) - 1), in percent: the sector's relative line against its own trailing 13-week average. Above 0 the sector is outperforming its own recent relative trend; below 0 it is underperforming it.",
  "rs_momentum": "RS-Momentum = RS-Ratio minus its own trailing 4-week average (SMA4w), in percentage points: above 0 the ratio has been rising over the last four weeks.",
  "quadrants": "Leading = ratio >= 0 and momentum >= 0; Weakening = ratio >= 0, momentum < 0; Lagging = both < 0; Improving = ratio < 0, momentum >= 0. The crosshair sits at 0/0 and sectors rotate clockwise, as on a classic relative-rotation graph.",
  "quadrant_weeks": "Consecutive weeks the sector has spent in its current quadrant.",
  "consistency": "Share of the last 30 quadrant weeks spent in the sector's most frequent (modal) quadrant, in percent.",
  "rotation_score": "RS-Ratio + RS-Momentum: summed distance from the 0/0 centre. rotation_rank orders sectors by it; rank_change_1w is last week's rank minus today's (positive = climbed).",
  "turnover_share": "Sector turnover (archive-reported; volume x close where a bar lacks a turnover figure) as a share of total turnover across sector-mapped equities, latest session. flow_shift_pp = latest share minus the trailing 120-session mean share, in percentage points.",
  "trail": "The last 12 weekly points of (RS-Ratio, RS-Momentum), one per week from the same weekly series as the head \u2014 the path the sector traced across the quadrants.",
  "quadrant_chart": "The chart at the top of the page is a separate, daily mechanism (see the board's quadrant_chart block): x = EMA5 of the RS line's 20-session change in %, y = the 5-session change of x. It answers 'where does each sector sit right now on a 20-day view'; the table's weekly posture answers the slower 13-week question. The two can disagree on a sector whose very recent sessions diverge from its weekly trend \u2014 that disagreement is information, not an error."
 },
