  "Rotation is a relative-strength map, not a buy or sell signal: a sector can lead while falling, if it falls less than the index.",
  "Construction changed 2026-10-23: the board previously used a daily JdK-style equivalent (100-centred, EMA50/SMA10 on sessions); it now uses the weekly mechanism described above, which tracks the reference board's published values (ratio sign agreement 11/11, quadrant agreement 10/11 on 2026-10-16 \u2014 Finance's momentum sits within a third of a point of zero on both boards).",
  "The quadrant chart (top of the page) is a separate daily mechanism decoded from the reference chart's own published spec \u2014 '20-day relative strength, 5-day smoothed' \u2014 and fitted against its 2026-10-16 dots: relative-strength sign agreement 7/7 on the readable sectors, quadrant agreement 5/7 (Non Life Insurance and Life Insurance land one quadrant apart, because the final sessions moved our equal-weight baskets differently from the reference's cap-weighted sub-indices). The table below it is the weekly posture; the two are labelled separately and are not expected to agree sector-for-sector."
